{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "The current best (config_012: pca_n2000 + ViT-L + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.6352) establishes that multiprofile + ViT-L + weighted fusion is the strongest combination. The two main untested levers are (a) aggregation method (avgpool vs. transformer) and (b) RNA encoder (PCA vs. learned scvi/scgpt). I choose config_015, which is a clean single-variable change from the current best—swapping avgpool for transformer aggregation while keeping pca_n2000, ViT-L, and weighted fusion fixed. This directly tests whether a learned, attention-based aggregation of multiprofile representations can outperform the simple mean-pooling that has been the default. If transformer aggregation captures non-uniform profile importance, it could push accuracy above 0.635; if not, we rule out that direction cheaply and pivot to RNA-encoder exploration (scgpt/scvi) in the remaining budget. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds self-attention compute over the profile set, so I estimate roughly 10–14 GPU hours—moderate, well within the remaining budget of ~51 GPU hours, and justified by the high information value of resolving the aggregation question before committing later experiments to a fixed aggregation strategy."
}

